# Release owners. Combined with the `protected-branches` ruleset's "Require review from Code Owners"
# (master and release/**), a PR that touches any of these paths needs an approving review from one of
# them. Changing `version` in gradle.properties drives the automatic tag and release, and the other
# paths decide what runs, with the release credentials, when it does.
#
# There is intentionally no catch-all `*` rule: all other paths stay unowned and do NOT require these
# reviewers. CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins, so keep the patterns below non-overlapping. Keep the owner
# list in sync with the workflow_dispatch allow-list in .github/workflows/tag-release.yml and the
# reviewers of the `release` and `github-pages` environments.

# This file, so the protection can't be removed without a release owner.
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @satran004 @fabianbormann @matiwinnetou

# Every workflow runs with the repository's secrets once it is on a protected branch.
/.github/workflows/      @satran004 @fabianbormann @matiwinnetou

# Version bump -> automatic tag and release.
/gradle.properties       @satran004 @fabianbormann @matiwinnetou

# Build logic evaluated by the credentialed release job: publication scope, signing, nmcp, and the
# Gradle distribution that runs it.
/build.gradle            @satran004 @fabianbormann @matiwinnetou
/settings.gradle         @satran004 @fabianbormann @matiwinnetou
/gradle/wrapper/         @satran004 @fabianbormann @matiwinnetou
/gradlew                 @satran004 @fabianbormann @matiwinnetou
/gradlew.bat             @satran004 @fabianbormann @matiwinnetou
